# Read by ESP-IDF as a component Kconfig, and by both forges' `make menu`
# (scripts/menu.py) for the STEPPER_<CHIP> prompts. stm-forge has no Kconfig
# build step: its build only sees the defconfig lines, as
# -DCONFIG_STEPPER_<CHIP>=1 or 0. Every chip is off unless set.
# Outside ESP-IDF, CMakeLists.txt takes its options from the bool entries
# here, found by their type line: keep `bool` directly under each `config`.
menuconfig STEPPER
    bool "Stepper driver subsystem"
    default y
    help
        The stepper core: struct stepper_dev, stepper_enable(),
        stepper_set_current(), stepper_read_status() and the stepper_* log
        helpers. Pick the chip drivers you need below; none is built by
        default, so a chip missing from sdkconfig is off.

if STEPPER

    config STEPPER_TMC2209
        bool "ADI/Trinamic TMC2209 (single-wire UART, velocity)"
        default n
        help
            Build the TMC2209 driver: tmc2209_init() and friends. The UART
            is the app's to install and configure.

    config STEPPER_TMC5240
        bool "ADI/Trinamic TMC5240 (SPI, ramp generator)"
        default n
        help
            Build the TMC5240 driver: tmc5240_init() and friends.

    config STEPPER_DEBUG
        bool "stepper_dbg() lines"
        default n
        help
            STM32 HAL only: compile stepper_dbg() lines in. On ESP-IDF
            stepper_dbg() is ESP_LOGD and the log level decides.

endif # STEPPER
